---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Documentation — Cutline">
  <h1>Documentation</h1>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      Complete documentation, FAQ, and technical reference for Cutline cut path DNS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <nav class="doc-nav">
    <a href="#what-is-cutline">What is Cutline?</a>
    <a href="#what-is-narge">What is Narge?</a>
    <a href="#how-it-works">How It Works</a>
    <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
    <a href="#limitations">Limitations</a>
    <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
    <a href="#technical">Technical Details</a>
    <a href="#contributing">Contributing</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="what-is-cutline">
    <h2>What is Cutline?</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline is the public Narge domain list and feed infrastructure. Organizations load the Narge list 
      into their own firewalls, DNS servers, or security platforms—Cutline provides the list.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cutline is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Open source and publicly documented</li>
      <li>No signup, no charge, no accounts</li>
      <li>Maintained by <a href="https://github.com/dov-max" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dov Allison</a></li>
      <li>Feed-first: you control your own DNS</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cutline is not a house product, safety brand, trust mark, government program, or kids-specific service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-is-narge">
    <h2>What is Narge?</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Narge</strong> (pronounced NARJ) is a technical content class. It is narrowly defined 
      in the <a href="/spec">Narge specification</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The classification looks at purpose and content type. It does not include CSAM (already illegal), 
      written-only text, non-photoreal illustration, medical content, sex education, news, documentary, 
      breastfeeding, clothing sales, or story films when purpose is not arousal.
    </p>
    <p>
      See the full <a href="/spec">Narge specification</a> for the complete definition and what is included or excluded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works">
    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    
    <h3>Feed-First Approach</h3>
    <p>
      Organizations load the Narge list into their own infrastructure:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Your firewall or DNS server fetches the Narge list from <code>https://feeds.thecutline.org</code></li>
      <li>Your own infrastructure checks incoming requests against the list</li>
      <li>Blocked domains return <code>NXDOMAIN</code> (domain does not exist) or are blocked at the firewall</li>
      <li>Everything else resolves normally through your chosen upstream DNS</li>
    </ol>
    
    <p>
      <strong>Deployment:</strong> See <a href="/for-it">For IT Teams</a> for platform-specific setup instructions.
    </p>

    <h3>What Gets Blocked</h3>
    <p>
      The Narge hostname list is published at <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dov-max/narge-spec</a>. 
      The list was seeded once from the <a href="https://github.com/StevenBlack/hosts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">StevenBlack hosts list subset</a> 
      (MIT license) and is now maintained as a curated hostname feed.
    </p>

    <h3>Your Traffic</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Important:</strong> Only DNS queries go through your own DNS infrastructure. Your actual web traffic 
      (loading pages, downloading files) goes directly from your device to the destination server.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline collects no personal data. Query names are not stored—after a query completes, the operator 
      cannot retrieve what was asked. The only retained data is source IP for 7 days (for rate limits and 
      public usage statistics), then deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong><a href="/privacy">Read the full privacy policy →</a></strong>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="limitations">
    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    
    <h3>Not Comprehensive</h3>
    <p>
      The Narge list addresses only one narrow content class. It does not block:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Malware or phishing sites (use additional security tools)</li>
      <li>Social media content (sexual or otherwise)</li>
      <li>Dating or hookup apps</li>
      <li>Other content categories (violence, gambling, etc.)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Easy to Bypass</h3>
    <p>
      Someone who wants to access blocked content can:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Change their DNS settings back to default</li>
      <li>Use a VPN or proxy</li>
      <li>Use mobile data instead of Wi-Fi</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cutline makes Narge harder to reach by accident or habit, not impossible to find.
    </p>

    <h3>List Quality</h3>
    <p>
      The block list is a curated hostname feed maintained by one steward. It is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Purpose-based, not content-scanning</li>
      <li>Subject to false positives and false negatives</li>
      <li>Manually maintained with a malware bar (incomplete coverage is expected)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Report false positives via <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issues</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>HTTPS Cannot Be Categorized</h3>
    <p>
      DNS blocking only works at the domain level. HTTPS content on general-purpose platforms 
      (Twitter, Reddit, Imgur) cannot be addressed by DNS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    
    <h3>Sites Won't Load</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Verify your firewall or DNS server successfully loaded the Narge list</li>
      <li>Check that devices have renewed their DHCP leases</li>
      <li>Flush DNS cache on client devices</li>
      <li>Verify no VPN or proxy is overriding DNS on individual devices</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Blocked Sites Still Load</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Verify DNS configuration with the <a href="/verify">verification probe</a></li>
      <li>Check for VPN usage on client devices</li>
      <li>Ensure devices are using DHCP and not static DNS settings</li>
      <li>The site may not be in the block list</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>List Not Updating</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Check your platform's external list fetch logs</li>
      <li>Verify the feed URL is correct: <code>https://feeds.thecutline.org/v1/narge.txt</code></li>
      <li>Report persistent issues on <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="technical">
    <h2>Technical Details</h2>
    
    <h3>Feed URLs</h3>
    <pre><code>https://feeds.thecutline.org/v1/narge.txt
https://feeds.thecutline.org/v1/narge-wildcard.txt
https://feeds.thecutline.org/v1/narge.rpz
https://feeds.thecutline.org/v1/narge-adguard.txt</code></pre>
    <p>
      See <a href="/for-it">For IT Teams</a> for all available formats and per-organization feed URLs.
    </p>

    <h3>Software Stack</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Feed Worker:</strong> Cloudflare Workers</li>
      <li><strong>List Source:</strong> Narge hostname feed (dist/narge.txt)</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> IP-free counter, no Worker logs</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>List Refresh</h3>
    <p>
      The list is updated daily via GitHub Actions and deployed automatically to the feed infrastructure.
    </p>

    <h3>Response for Blocked Domains</h3>
    <p>
      Blocked domains return <code>NXDOMAIN</code> (DNS response code 3) when enforced by your own DNS server, 
      or are blocked at the firewall depending on your deployment method.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contributing">
    <h2>Contributing</h2>
    
    <h3>Report Issues</h3>
    <p>
      Found a problem? Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Propose Host Changes</h3>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue templates</a> 
      to propose:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A host to add to the block list</li>
      <li>A host to remove (false positive)</li>
      <li>A new host type or classification rule</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Improve Documentation</h3>
    <p>
      Documentation is in the <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener">narge-spec repository</a>. 
      Pull requests welcome.
    </p>

    <h3>Run Your Own</h3>
    <p>
      The resolver configuration is open source. <a href="/run-your-own">Deploy your own cut path</a> 
      and share it with others.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>GitHub:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open an issue</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Maintainer:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/dov-max" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dov Allison</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .doc-nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .doc-nav a {
    padding: var(--spacing-xs) var(--spacing-md);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }

  .doc-nav a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  section {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  ul, ol {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  blockquote {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  pre {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: #f8f8f2;
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }

  pre code {
    color: #f8f8f2;
  }

  code {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .contact {
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--spacing-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .contact h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .doc-nav {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
</style>
